{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Right or left.</b> Even if he tells you that right is left or that left is right — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 17:11). Its meaning is: even if you think in your heart that they are mistaken, and the matter is plain in your eyes just as you know your right from your left, you must still act in accordance with their command. And do not say, \"How can I eat this utterly forbidden fat?\" or \"How can I put to death this innocent man?\" Rather, say: \"Thus the Master who commands the commandments has commanded me to act in all His commandments according to all that they instruct me — those who stand before Him in the place that He shall choose — and upon the authority of their understanding He has given me the Torah, even if they err.\" This is like the matter of Rabbi Joshua with Rabban Gamliel concerning Yom Kippur that fell on their reckoning (Rosh Hashanah 25a). And the need for this commandment is very great, for the Torah was given to us in writing, and it is known that opinions will not be equal in all matters that arise. Disputes would multiply and the Torah would become many Torot, so the verse has cut short for us: the law is that we heed the Great Court that stands before HaShem in the place that He shall choose, in everything they tell us concerning the interpretation of the Torah — whether they received its interpretation as tradition from witness by witness and Moses from the mouth of the Almighty, or whether they say so according to the plain sense of the verse or its intention. For upon their understanding He gives the Torah to them [variant: to us], even if it seems in your eyes as though they are swapping right for left, and all the more so when you ought to consider that they are saying of right that it is right — for the spirit of HaShem is upon the ministers of His sanctuary, and He will not forsake His devout ones forever; they are preserved from error and from stumbling. And the language of Sifrei (Shofetim 154) is: even if it appears in your eyes that right is left and that left is right, listen to them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {0 "I resolved 'ר\"ג' as Rabban Gamliel and 'הגבורה' as 'the Almighty,' both standard identifications. The variant reading flagged by the editor (ס\"א לנו = 'one version: to us') is rendered in brackets. The Sifrei citation 'קנד' (= 154 in standard numbering) is left as the equivalenced number."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:51:16.305160932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}